---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description={`Privacy policy for ${site.name}.`}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>{site.name} respects your privacy and handles personal information in line with the Australian Privacy Principles under the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth).</p>
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you contact us, submit a form or book online, we collect the details you provide, such as your name, phone number, email and information about your health concern.</p>
      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>We use your information to respond to your enquiry, arrange and manage appointments, provide care, and improve our services. We don’t sell your personal information.</p>
      <h2>Website analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>Our website uses cookies and similar tools from Meta (the Meta Pixel) and Google to understand how visitors use the site and to measure and show our ads, including to people who have visited our site. We may also share contact details you’ve given us, in a secure scrambled (hashed) form, with Meta or Google to show you relevant ads. These companies may store data overseas. You can manage this in your browser settings or your Facebook and Google ad preferences.</p>
      <p>We only send marketing emails or SMS if you’ve agreed to receive them, and you can unsubscribe at any time.</p>
      <h2>Health information</h2>
      <p>Clinical records are stored securely in our practice management system and are only accessed by authorised team members involved in your care.</p>
      <h2>Access and correction</h2>
      <p>You can ask to access or correct the personal information we hold about you by contacting us on {site.phone} or {site.email}.</p>
      <h2>Complaints</h2>
      <p>If you have a concern about how we’ve handled your information, please contact us on {site.phone} or {site.email} and we’ll work with you to resolve it.</p>
      <p class="fine-print">Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-AU', { month: 'long', year: 'numeric' })}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>.prose h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-top: 1.6em; }</style>
